Um, I'd disagree with that one on empirical grounds.  I've mentioned
from time to time that I sometimes back up game files.  In keeping
with the newsgroup customs, I won't post ascension data from any
ascension that results from a saved file.  People have suggested that
I use Explore mode instead, but they've been pretty mild about it.

I think the current flap shows that rgrn chases away players who 1)
insist that savescumming is the best way to play or 2) insist that
everyone else does it and lies about it.  I think both of those are
perfectly reasonable.

For me, Explore mode doesn't provide a reasonable alternative to
savescumming.  My view on save files is to think of it as an alternate
universe with branching points.  I'll generally save when I'm in a
tight spot, to see which of a few possible options will get me out of
it.  I have the computer set up to suppress all the DYWYPI info when I
do that, so I won't be tempted to look.  And sometimes there isn't a
way out, at which point I acknowledge that, and delete the file.  

And for Alexis, I always manually delete bones files that are
generated as a result of savescumming, so it doesn't affect my Hearse
files.

